.env
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# data/raw and data/processed are DVC's from M1-S2 on: `dvc add` wrote them into
# data/.gitignore, which is the tracked, authoritative entry. Repeating them here
# would be twins — and a stale copy here would keep hiding the data even if the
# DVC tracking were removed by accident, which is exactly the failure you want loud.
# The DuckDB catalogue is regenerable: `make duckdb`.
data/analyst.duckdb
data/analyst.duckdb.wal
# Row-level model predictions (M2-S4). Ignored HERE and not by DVC, on purpose:
# they are MODEL OUTPUT, regenerable by `make predictions` in ~4 minutes from
# DVC-pinned inputs plus a registry version. A .dvc pin would have to be
# refreshed every time the champion moves (M3's bake-off, M7's retrains) — a pin
# that is stale by design is worse than no pin, because it looks like provenance.
# The real provenance is data/predictions/predictions.json plus the registry.
data/predictions/
# The champion's rows on the SCORING months (M7-S2), on identical terms and for
# identical reasons: model output, regenerable by `make predictions-scoring`
# from a DVC-pinned scoring tree plus a registry version, provenance in
# data/scoring_predictions/scoring_predictions.json plus the registry. A fourth
# tree and not a subdirectory of the third — see configs/train.yaml for why a
# 2020 file under data/predictions/ would reach the error_segments mart.
data/scoring_predictions/
# `make contract-probe`'s throwaway acquisition directory (M7-S1). The probe
# downloads a REAL TLC file to measure what the contract says about it, then
# writes nothing else — so these bytes are not data this program owns, and they
# are deliberately not DVC-tracked either. data/raw stays the only acquisition
# the manifest pins.
data/probe/
mlruns/
.dvc/cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
*.egg-info/
notebooks/*.ipynb_checkpoints/
.idea/
automation/logs/
automation/STOP

# dbt's build artifacts are regenerable: `make marts`. marts.duckdb is a
# rebuildable copy of aggregates whose source (data/processed) is DVC-pinned, so
# it is not a second thing to version — it is a cache with a build command.
analytics/dbt/marts.duckdb
analytics/dbt/marts.duckdb.wal
analytics/dbt/target/
analytics/dbt/logs/
analytics/dbt/dbt_packages/

# verify-m1's throwaway sandbox: the corrupt-parquet red-team writes its fixture
# here, under a throwaway config, so a corrupt byte never goes near data/raw.
# The gate deletes it on exit; this entry covers a run that was interrupted.
.verify_m1_sandbox/

# automation/runs/ — the records two milestone gates REPLAY (F-029, decided at the
# M4 boundary 2026-08-19, option A). The verdict JSONs are the evidence base of
# `verify-m3` §5 and `verify-m4` §3-§6, and both red teams simulate an EDITED
# record — so what a gate reads must be what review can see, or a tampered record
# lands with no diff for anybody to notice. The JSONs are therefore TRACKED; the
# logs and .status files stay ignored (they are transcripts, they are large, and
# no gate reads them).
#
# The three rules below are one mechanism, not three preferences. A bare
# `automation/runs/` exclusion makes git stop descending into the directory, and
# a `!` rule underneath it then does NOTHING — so the exclusion is pattern-based
# (`/**`), the directories are re-included (`!.../**/`) so git keeps walking, and
# the JSONs are re-included last.
automation/runs/**
!automation/runs/**/
!automation/runs/**/*.json

# ---- M8: the Feast quarantine (M8-S2) ----
# `.venv-feast` is an ISOLATED interpreter holding feast 0.66.0 and pandas 2.3.3
# against this project's pandas 3.0.5 — the wall M8 law 4 measured. uv writes its
# own `.gitignore` inside a venv it creates, so this entry is not strictly needed;
# it is here so the exclusion is visible in the file a reviewer opens (F-029's
# lesson: what a gate reads must be what review can see).
.venv-feast/
# The parquet Feast reads: derived read-only from the settled trees by
# `make feast-sources`, regenerable by one command, and NOT DVC-tracked for
# data/predictions/'s reason exactly — a pin that must be refreshed whenever an
# upstream tree moves is provenance that lies.
data/feast/
# Feast's local registry and sqlite online store. GENERATED: the definitions in
# infra/feast/feature_repo/definitions.py are the source of truth, and a registry
# committed beside them would be the second home F-013 keeps deleting.
infra/feast/feature_repo/data/
